<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Functions in Real Life — modelling a filling water tank</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A water tank starts with {@start@} litres of water. A tap fills it at a constant rate of {@rate@} litres per minute.</p>
<ol class="tb-parts">
  <li><p>Write a function \(V(t)\) for the volume of water, in litres, after \(t\) minutes.</p>
    <div>\(V(t) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div></li>
  <li><p>Use your function to find the volume after {@tval@} minutes.</p>
    <div>\(V({@tval@}) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] litres [[feedback:prt2]]</div></li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<ol class="tb-parts">
  <li><p>The volume changes at a constant rate, so \(V\) is a <strong>linear function</strong> of \(t\): \(V(t) = (\text{starting amount}) + (\text{rate})\times t\). The starting amount {@start@} litres is the constant term, the value of \(V\) when \(t = 0\). The rate {@rate@} litres per minute is the gradient, so it multiplies \(t\):</p>
  \[ V(t) = {@ta1@}. \]</li>
  <li><p>Substitute \(t = {@tval@}\):</p>
  \[ V({@tval@}) = {@start@} + {@rate@}\times{@tval@} = {@ta2@}\ \text{litres}. \]</li>
</ol>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Straight-line graph of volume V against time t, starting at the initial volume on the V-axis, with the point at the given time marked.">
[[jsxgraph width="360px" height="240px"]]
(function() {
  var V0 = {#start#}, r = {#rate#}, T = {#tval#}, VT = {#ta2#};
  var tmax = T + 3, vmax = V0 + r*tmax;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-0.12*tmax, 1.15*vmax, 1.08*tmax, -0.12*vmax], axis: true, grid: false,
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false
  });
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(t){ return V0 + r*t; }, 0, tmax], {strokeColor:'#003399', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('point', [0, V0], {size:3, color:'#006600', fixed:true, name:'start ' + V0, label:{offset:[8,-12], anchorX:'left'}});
  b.create('segment', [[T, 0], [T, VT]], {strokeColor:'#888888', dash:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('point', [T, VT], {size:4, color:'#cc0000', fixed:true, name:'(' + T + ', ' + VT + ')', label:{offset:[-10,10], anchorX:'right'}});
  b.create('text', [1.0*tmax, 0.06*vmax, 't'], {anchorX:'right', fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [0.02*tmax, 1.08*vmax, 'V'], {fixed:true});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
